This patch adds an option, trap_on_top, which enables you to toggle
whether traps are displayed above or below objects. In addition, I
added the command "%" (it looks a bit like one object on top of
another, and it's adjacent to ^ on my keyboard) to toggle this option
quickly for use in play - so you can easily check if an object has a
known trap under it or vice versa.

(Unfortunately, the "%" command forces a full screen redraw leading to
noticable flicker. There's no way round this.)

The "YAASD deadly poison pit" earlier today (in which somebody fell
into a pit obscured by a freakin' dagger) finally inspired me to write
a patch for this, since it has always annoyed me that objects obscure
traps from your vision - especially since traps tend to acquire objects
(dart traps, arrow traps, pits in which monsters have died and dropped
stuff, landmines in Ludios).

This is my first patch, so it may not work! Please let me know how you
get on with it. I've changed everything relevant except the Guidebooks
(cmdhelp and opthelp have been updated).

Philip

